.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt PROC_TERMINATE 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm proc_terminate
.Nd terminate a process
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ft int
.Fn proc_terminate "Handle proc" "int code"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The .Nm system call terminates the process referred to by
.Fa proc and all of its threads, and stores
.Fa code as the exit status observed by
.Xr proc_wait 2 .
The caller must hold the
.Dv SIGNAL
right on
.Fa proc ;
process handles created by
.Xr proc_create 2
carry it, and it can be passed with
.Xr handle_dup 2
or
.Xr handle_transfer 2 .
.Pp
Terminating the calling process is equivalent to
.Xr exit 2 .
Terminating a process that is already terminal fails with
.Er ESRCH .
The call only requests termination; the target may still be tearing
down when .Nm returns, which .Xr proc_wait 2 observes.
.Pp
This page documents the native RavenBSD ABI; see the
.Pa raven-abi
crate for the exact numeric value and types.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
On success .Nm returns 0; on failure it returns a negative error number.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Er EBADF
.Fa proc
is not a valid process handle.
.It Er EPERM
The caller does not hold the
.Dv SIGNAL
right on
.Fa proc .
.It Er ESRCH
The target process is already terminal.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr exit 2 ,
.Xr proc_create 2 ,
.Xr proc_wait 2
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
